osts and Affordability Tuition and Fees Housing and Dining Financial Aid Meet the Student Financial Services Team Financial Aid Process Scholarships and Financial Aid Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Deadlines Information for Veterans Contact Admissions Schedule an Appointment Meet Your Counselor Admission Events Campus Tours Counselor Resources Student Life Resources Agency for Civic Engagement Art Galleries ASWU Center for Entrepreneurship Fashion Study Collection Honors Program Julius Shulman Institute Making Complex Materials Library Wedge Gallery WU Radio Living Safety & Security Student Experience Dining Student Housing Student Services URReading Therapy Services Sustainability on Campus Student Success Initiatives The CARE Team Academic Support Health and Wellness Services for Students with Disabilities Career Services International Students Academic Advising Catalog Los Angeles Times Library Academic Calendar International Students Merch Store About About Woodbury Inclusiveness & Community Community Outreach and Engagement Committee Why Woodbury? Parents and Families Strategic Direction: Facts and Figures History Our Location News Accreditations For Employers Filming, Conferences, and Events People Faculty Directory Administration Contact Us Partners Careers Campus Map Campus Tours Merch Store Contacts Alumni Giving Apply Undergraduate Graduate Tour Virtual Tour Campus Tours Students Academic Calendars Associated Students Bookstore Catalog Complaint Resolution Process Health & Wellness International Students The Los Angeles Times Library Making Complex Reservation-LA Math, Science & Subject Tutoring Center Merch Store Canvas Commencement 2026 Order Transcripts Parking Permits Portal Self-Service Student Handbook Student Job Board Woody's Info Writing Center Faculty/Staff Academic Calendars Bookstore Catalog The Los Angeles Times Library Merch Store Canvas Portal Self-Service Woody's Info News & Events Latest News Upcoming Events Parents & Families Frequently Asked Questions SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) Welcome to University of Redlands, Los Angeles (formerly Woodbury University) SOAR! We are excited to welcome you to the University of Redlands family. Our SOAR program is designed to help you start your journey with confidence and excitement. Mark Your Calendars University of Redlands, Los Angeles’ next in-person SOAR will be held on Friday, August 28th : – New Student Move-In: 8:00 AM – 10:00 AM – New Student and Family Orientation: 10:00 AM – 4:30 PM *Schedule is subject to change An orientation fee will be included on your student account. What to Expect from SOAR SOAR is a multi-part event designed to introduce you to University of Redlands, Los Angeles and help you transition smoothly. Step 1: Pre-SOAR Before registering for classes, please complete the following: Online SOAR Modules Beginning June, you will have access to exciting online SOAR modules to help orient you to campus before arriving in person. You will receive a link via email on how to log into Canvas and Navigate360 to complete the online modules. After completing the modules, you will be directed to register for courses. New Student Checklist Also, through your Navigate360 portal, you will be able to review all necessary deadlines for required documentation and forms. You can submit these through Navigate360. Step 2: Register for Classes After completing the necessary New Student Checklist items on Navigate360, you will be able to meet with your Student Success Advisor to discuss which courses to take. From there, you and your advisor will build your schedule together, and you will register for classes. Step 3: In-Person SOAR Visit campus to tour the facilities, meet your faculty, register for classes, and learn how to make the most of your time at University of Redlands, Los Angeles. RSVP links will also be included through the Navigate360 portal. In-person SOAR is mandatory for all new students, including transfer students and graduate students. We look forward to meeting you! University of Redlands, Los Angeles SOAR Schedule Below you can find the schedule for the upcoming student orientation advising and registration event happening August 28, 2026. Undergraduate Students Time Event 8:00–10:30 AM Housing Move-In 8:30–10:30 AM Check-In 9:00 AM Campus Tour (Optional) 9:00 AM Math Placement Assessment (if needed) 10:30–11:15 AM Welcome Session 11:15–12:00 PM Campus Challenge 12:00–1:00PM Title IX Education 1:00–1:45 PM Lunch 1:45 –2:30 PM Student Success & Belonging 2:30–3:00 PM Meet Your Department 3:00–4:00 PM Resource Fair & Campus Connections 3:00–4:00 PM Final Reception & Swag 4:00–5:00 PM Individual Appointments (as needed) 6:00–8:00 PM New Student Mixer (Optional) Graduate Students Time Event 8:00–10:30AM Housing Move-In 8:30–10:30 AM Check-In 9:00AM Campus Tour (Optional) 10:30–11:15 AM Welcome Session 11:15–12:00 PM Meet Your Department 12:00–1:00PM Lunch 1:00–3:00 PM (Optional) Advising / Registration / Faculty Meetings / Departure 3:00–4:00 PM Resource Fair (Optional) 4:00–5:00 PM Individual Appointments (Optional) 6:00–8:00 PM New Student Mixer (Optional) tableing 6 Family Session While students are on campus, families can attend dedicated sessions to learn how to support their students during this transition. Parents & Families Time Event 8:00–10:30AM Housing Move-In 8:30–10:30 AM Check-In 9:00AM Campus Tour (Optional) 10:30–11:15 AM Welcome Session 11:15–12:00 PM What Families Need to Know 12:00–1:00PM Parent Breakout Sessions 12:45PM Lunch 1:45 –2:30 PM Campus Resources in Action 2:30–3:00 PM Letting Go While Staying Connected:  A Conversation with Parents 3:00–4:00 PM Resource Fair 3:00–4:00 PM Final Reception & Swag 4:00–5:00 PM Individual Appointments (Optional) Celebrate Your Future We’re looking forward to welcoming you onto campus and sharing all the information to get you ready to start the next steps in your education! Student Discounts As you prepare for the new school year, take advantage of these limited-time student discounts. IKEA: 15% Off One Purchase IKEA is offering verified college and university students 15% off one purchase through September 30, 2026. Access the offer through the IKEA College Student Discount page . Students must join or log in to the free IKEA Family program and complete the online student verification process. Once verified, students will receive a one-time coupon code. Target: 20% Off One Purchase Target is offering students 20% off one entire purchase through September 12, 2026. This discount may be used only once. To access the discount: Open the ​ Target student discount flyer ​ and scan the QR code. Download or open the Target app. Create or verify your student account. Locate the 20% student discount on the app’s home page. Frequently Asked Questions What is SOAR? SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) helps new students transition into University of Redlands, Los Angeles (formerly Woodbury University) and get started successfully. Is SOAR required? Yes. All new students must complete online SOAR modules and attend in-person SOAR. Can my family attend SOAR? Yes. Up to two guests may accompany you. Do international students need to attend SOAR? Yes. In addition to SOAR, international students must attend International Student Orientation to learn about legal requirements and responsibilities. Meet Your SOAR Team University of Redlands, Los Angeles’ SOAR team is here to help with any questions or concerns you may have. Evetth Gonzalez Dean of Students & Success Elizabeth “Lisa” Cooper Associate Registrar Morgan Queen Student Affairs Administrative Assistant Nina Lam Instructional Designer – IT E-mail: urla_orientation@redlands.edu Phone: 818.252.5117 Admissions Undergraduate Why URLA? Applying to University Redlands Los Angeles Transfer Students International Applicants Veteran Applicants Undocumented Applicants Undergraduate Admitted Students SOAR (Student Orientatio