      "title": "Ask an URLA Student",
      "description": "Ask an URLA Student - Woodbury University Skip to main content Enable accessibility for low vision Open the accessibility menu Students Academic Calendars Associated Students Bookstore Catalog Complaint Resolution Process Health & Wellness International Students The Los Angeles Times Library Making Complex Reservation-LA Math, Science & Subject Tutoring Center Merch Store Canvas Commencement 2026 Order Transcripts Parking Permits Portal Self-Service Student Handbook Student Job Board Woody's Info Writing Center Faculty/Staff Academic Calendars Bookstore Catalog The Los Angeles Times Library Merch Store Canvas Portal Self-Service Woody's Info News & Events Latest News Upcoming Events Parents & Families Frequently Asked Questions Search Apply Academics Woodbury School of Design and Media Arts Center for Interdisciplinary Studies Woodbury School of Architecture Woodbury Business Institute Undergraduate Accounting Animation + VFX Architecture BBA-MBA Accelerated Program Computer Information Systems Construction Management Fashion Design Fashion Marketing Filmmaking, BA Filmmaking, BFA Game Art & Design Graphic + Experience Design Interdisciplinary Studies Interior Design Management Marketing Public Safety Administration Graduate BBA-MBA Accelerated Program Master of Architecture Master of Business Administration (MBA) Master of Interior Design Master of Science in Architecture Master’s in Interdisciplinary Design Internships List of Minors Catalog Academic Calendar Los Angeles Times Library Admissions Undergraduate Why URLA? Applying to University Redlands Los Angeles Transfer Students International Applicants Veteran Applicants Undocumented Applicants Undergraduate Admitted Students SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) Readmission Ask an URLA Student Graduate Readmission Applying to Graduate Programs Graduate Transfer Requirements International Applicants Veteran Applicants Graduate Admitted Students Costs and Affordability Tuition and Fees Housing and Dining Financial Aid Meet the Student Financial Services Team Financial Aid Process Scholarships and Financial Aid Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Deadlines Information for Veterans Contact Admissions Schedule an Appointment Meet Your Counselor Admission Events Campus Tours Counselor Resources Student Life Resources Agency for Civic Engagement Art Galleries ASWU Center for Entrepreneurship Fashion Study Collection Honors Program Julius Shulman Institute Making Complex Materials Library Wedge Gallery WU Radio Living Safety & Security Student Experience Dining Student Housing Student Services URReading Therapy Services Sustainability on Campus Student Success Initiatives The CARE Team Academic Support Health and Wellness Services for Students with Disabilities Career Services International Students Academic Advising Catalog Los Angeles Times Library Academic Calendar International Students Merch Store About About Woodbury Inclusiveness & Community Community Outreach and Engagement Committee Why Woodbury? Parents and Families Strategic Direction: Facts and Figures History Our Location News Accreditations For Employers Filming, Conferences, and Events People Faculty Directory Administration Contact Us Partners Careers Campus Map Campus Tours Merch Store Contacts Alumni Giving Apply Undergraduate Graduate Tour Virtual Tour Campus Tours Students Academic Calendars Associated Students Bookstore Catalog Complaint Resolution Process Health & Wellness International Students The Los Angeles Times Library Making Complex Reservation-LA Math, Science & Subject Tutoring Center Merch Store Canvas Commencement 2026 Order Transcripts Parking Permits Portal Self-Service Student Handbook Student Job Board Woody's Info Writing Center Faculty/Staff Academic Calendars Bookstore Catalog The Los Angeles Times Library Merch Store Canvas Portal Self-Service Woody's Info News & Events Latest News Upcoming Events Parents & Families Frequently Asked Questions Ask an URLA Student Have a question about University of Redlands, Los Angeles? One of the best ways to learn about our amazing community is by communication with a current student! Please email us at urlaadmissions@redlands.edu and we’ll get back to you within 1-2 business days. Animation + VFX (Class of 2027) Arsine I come from : Yerevan, Armenia I speak : English and Armenian Clubs/groups you are involved in on campus : Woodbury Animation Club, ASA Favorite course(s): I personally really like the foundational animation courses (AVFX 100 and 101), along with beginning drawing (FOUN 101) and figure drawing (FOUN 105), because implementing the curriculum had aided in me being able to solidify my projects and has strengthened my skills as an artist. Favorite spot on campus and why : I love the library because it is the most aesthetically pleasing location on campus. I frequently go there to focus on my work and wind down as well. I also appreciate the history behind this library and how it was originally a church. The interior and exterior elements of the church are still present and make the library unique. Hobbies and Interests: Drawing, of course, is my main and favorite hobby; however, I also love content creation, making new templates for my small business, listening to music, and cooking. I chose to attend University of Redlands, Los Angeles (formerly Woodbury University) because: I am very local and the high school I attended is also in Burbank; therefore, I got a better look at the wonderful resources available for Woodbury’s animation program and saw that opportunities are more accessible due to the location. Many popular animation studios are located nearby! Additionally, I prefer a smaller campus with little class sizes since that helps me enhance my connections with professors and students. Psychology (class of 2027) Eva I come from North Hollywood, CA I speak English and Russian Clubs/groups you are involved in on-campus: Psychology club Favorite courses: I really enjoyed my Journeys (INDS 101) class with Professor Mike Sonksen because I got to dedicate time to learning more about my own life journey through journaling and reflection and I was able to take inspiration from my classmates and other artists we learned about. Favorite spot on campus and why: My favorite spot is Woody’s, our dining hall, because I feel like it is the heart of campus. I love getting some good food and looking at the art wall inside or looking out at the greenery of the quad when I sit on the patio. Hobbies/interests: I like rock climbing, writing, listening to music, learning new things, and spending time with my favorite people. I chose to attend University of Redlands, Los Angeles (formerly Woodbury University) because the small community allows me to bond with my peers and get one-on-one access to professors and faculty. I also love that Woodbury prioritizes giving students real-world experience through projects and internships before we even graduate. We all work together to help each other succeed. Psychology (Class of 2027) Kaylene I come from Pacoima, CA. I speak English Clubs/groups I’m a part of: I’m not currently part of any clubs or groups on campus, but I hope to be! Favorite Courses: My favorite course currently is PSYC 200 with Dr. Joye Swan. She keeps the class engaged, and I love learning about psychology. It is a great class, even if you are not a Psychology major because it gives you a broad overview of psychology and how humans interact with each other and the world around us. Taking this class, I will be able to specify how the principles of psychology can be used for everyday problems while bringing awareness to many different subjects psychology is involved in. Favorite spot on campus and why: My favorite spot is the Library. It’s my favorite spot because it’s a great place to study and because of the great history behind it. The Library used to be a chapel when this campus first was a school of girls founded by Mother Frances Xavier Cabrini and was called Villa Cabrini Academy. It’s a great reminder of the beginnings of this university and the importance of education to me. Along with the stained-glass windows and beautiful chandeliers, the library creates a feeling that we are all here to learn and develop into great scholars. Hobbies/ interests: I enjoy going to concerts and listening to music. I also like to go out social dancing with friends and go on road trips! I chose to attend University of Redlands, Los Angeles (formerly Woodbury University) because I wanted a smaller learning environment with my professors and peers. Here, I can fully expand my potential and learn to the best of my ability. Amazingly, professors and advisers can get one-on-one time with you to get real-world experience through internships and other opportunities tailored to me and my education. Animation + VFX (class of 2029) Paige I come from: La Canada Flintridge California I speak: English Clubs/groups your involved in on campus: Woodbury Animation Club Favorite Courses: I am personally fond of the Figure Drawing, Intro to Digital Media, and the Industry Insiders classes we have available here at Woodbury. They do an amazing job of teaching techniques and preparing students for the animation industry. Favorite spot on campus and why: My favorite spot on campus would have to be Woodies Cafeteria. It’s where at any point in my day, if I’m feeling down, I can visit, get some food, and spend time with my friends or piers from my classes. It is genuinely such an amazing community space that is always hosting events for students. Hobbies and Interests: I really enjoy drawing in my free time as well as playing video games such as Hollow Knight, Pokémon, and legend of Zelda.  I also enjoy hiking with friends and spending time outdoors. I choose to attend University of Redlands, Los Angeles (formerly Woodbury University) because: I was really impressed with the animation industry that is local to Burbank and wanted to stay within an hour drive of my hometown. On top of that I was interested in attending a smaller school like Woodbury to get to know my classmates more closely. However, what really sold me on the school was definitely the campus. When I toured the campus for the first time, I was swept away by the New York Times Library and the old brick buildings that surrounded the quad. I really loved how it was right up against the mountains and in a very safe suburban area. Admissions Undergraduate Why URLA? Applying to University Redlands Los Angeles Transfer Students International Applicants Veteran Applicants Undocumented Applicants Undergraduate Admitted Students SOAR (Student Orientation, Advising, and Registration) Readmission Ask an URLA Student Graduate Readmission Applying to Graduate Programs Domestic Applicants International Applicants Veteran Applicants Graduate Transfer Requirements International Applicants Veteran Applicants Graduate Admitted Students Costs and Affordability Tuition and Fees Housing and Dining Financial Aid Meet the Student Financial Services Team Financial Aid Process Scholarships and Financial Aid Financial Aid Resources Financial Aid Deadlines Information for Veterans Contact Admissions Schedule an Appointment Meet Your Counselor Admission Events Campus Tours Counselor Resources Contact Us To get in touch with us, please feel free to give the Admissions Office a call, send an email, or fill out the form. Thank you. Empty heading Los Angeles Campus Admissions Office 7500 N Glenoaks Blvd, Burbank, CA 91504 818 252 5221 | urlaadmissions@redlands.edu Request More Information Loading... * denotes a required field. What academic level are you interested in?* First-Year Transfer Graduate Contact Information First Name* Last Name* Email Address* Cell* Academic Information Institution you currently attend* CEEB (hidden) Academic Interest* Architecture Construction Management Interior Design Accounting Business (evening degree completion) Busines